---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of service — OpenKarta" activeNav={null}>
  <section class="max-w-[1440px] mx-auto px-8 md:px-16 mt-20 mb-16">
    <div class="font-label-caps text-label-caps uppercase mb-8 border border-on-background/20 bg-on-background/5 text-on-background inline-block px-3 py-1">Terms · effective 2026-04-26</div>
    <h1 class="font-hero-h1 text-on-background [font-size:clamp(48px,8vw,108px)] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight max-w-5xl">
      Terms of service.
    </h1>
    <p class="font-h2-editorial text-on-surface-variant mt-8 max-w-3xl">
      Plain language. The protocol is MIT — these terms govern only the OpenKarta-operated services (registry, API, marketing site).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-[1440px] mx-auto px-8 md:px-16 mb-32">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-8">
      <aside class="md:col-span-3 hidden md:block">
        <div class="font-label-caps text-label-caps uppercase text-on-surface-variant mb-4 sticky top-24">Sections</div>
        <ul class="space-y-2 sticky top-32">
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#scope">1. Scope</a></li>
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#use">2. Acceptable use</a></li>
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#listings">3. Registry listings</a></li>
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#liability">4. Disclaimers &amp; liability</a></li>
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#changes">5. Changes</a></li>
          <li><a class="font-body-dense text-body-dense text-on-surface-variant hover:text-on-background" href="#law">6. Governing law</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
      <article class="md:col-span-9 space-y-12">
        <section id="scope" class="border-b border-on-background/10 pb-8">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">1. Scope</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            These terms apply to the services operated by the OpenKarta foundation: the registry at <span class="font-code-block">registry.openkarta.org</span>, the public API at <span class="font-code-block">api.openkarta.org</span>, and the marketing site at <span class="font-code-block">openkarta.org</span>. The protocol packages on npm and the source code on GitHub are governed by their MIT license.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="use" class="border-b border-on-background/10 pb-8">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">2. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant mb-4">
            Don't abuse the public API. Reasonable rate limits apply (see headers on every response). Don't use the API to enumerate competitors' merchants for harassment. Don't impersonate a merchant in the registry submission flow.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            We may suspend abusive accounts or domains. Suspensions are reversible by emailing <a class="underline" href="mailto:hello@openkarta.org">hello@openkarta.org</a> with context.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="listings" class="border-b border-on-background/10 pb-8">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">3. Registry listings</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant mb-4">
            By submitting an agent for listing, you affirm you control the domain you submit, that the manifest you publish is accurate, and that you will keep the agent reachable enough to pass the conformance sweep. Failure to do so results in <span class="font-code-block">stale</span> and ultimately <span class="font-code-block">delisted</span> status.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            We do not act as a merchant of record. The merchant remains solely responsible for fulfillment, taxation, refunds, and dispute resolution with buyers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="liability" class="border-b border-on-background/10 pb-8">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">4. Disclaimers &amp; liability</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant mb-4">
            The services are provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. The protocol packages are MIT-licensed and carry the MIT warranty disclaimer. To the fullest extent permitted by law, OpenKarta is not liable for indirect, consequential, or special damages arising from use of the services.
          </p>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            Conformance badges are signed attestations of the registry runner's observations at a point in time. They are not warranties of merchant quality, fulfillment reliability, or product safety.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="changes" class="border-b border-on-background/10 pb-8">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">5. Changes</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced via the <a class="underline" href="/changelog">changelog</a> at least 14 days before they take effect.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="law">
          <h2 class="font-h2-editorial text-on-background mb-4">6. Governing law</h2>
          <p class="font-body-main text-body-main text-on-surface-variant">
            These terms are governed by the laws of India, where the foundation is incorporated. Disputes are resolved in the courts of Bengaluru, Karnataka.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
